      <div class="key-points">
        <h2>The short version</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Separate what you taste into four channels: <strong>aroma, palate, heat, finish</strong>. Most confusion comes from collapsing them into one verdict.</li>
          <li>Aroma type determines which flavour families are available. You will not find soy and mushroom in a light aroma, or pear and white flowers in a sauce aroma.</li>
          <li>"Strong" is not a flavour — it is usually a combination of alcohol heat and aromatic density. Naming which one changes your buying decision.</li>
          <li>Compare two bottles side by side. One bottle alone teaches you almost nothing.</li>
          <li>Write three words per bottle, not a score. The words are the skill.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

